  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of an important population of the Critically Endangered Southern River Terrapin,..Batagur affinis, in Southern Cambodia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of an important population of critically endangered Southern River Terrapin, Batagur affineis, in Southern Cambodia. In partnership with Wildlife Conservation Society, this project will improve the global conservation status of Batagur affinis by reducing threats to, and improving recruitment in an important remnant population in Cambodia. Specific activities include: (1) expand and increase effectiveness of patrols aimed at discovering additional nests using the SMART (Spatial Monitoring And Reporting Tool) method originally developed by WCS and USFWS for tiger conservation; (2) conduct in situ nest incubation and protection for all nests found in the wild that will be guarded by wardens; (3) transfer hatchling turtles from field incubation studies to head-starting facilities; (4) select and release 25 head-started turtles with an acoustic tag; (5) monitor turtles post release using an omni directional hydrophone and underwater automated recording stations.</narrative>
  </description>
